Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:00:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] generic: tag_rtl8366ub_8021q: reset MAC header after the
 trap strip

Add 795-13: after rtl8366ub_8021q_control_rcv() strips the RTL8_4
header, skb->mac_header still points at the old frame start, so
eth_hdr()->h_proto reads part of the destination MAC and an in-band
802.1Q tag on a trapped frame is missed. Reset the MAC header after
the strip, as tag_sja1105.c does.
---
 ...366ub_8021q-reset-MAC-header-after-s.patch | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/795-13-net-dsa-tag_rtl8366ub_8021q-reset-MAC-header-after-s.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/795-13-net-dsa-tag_rtl8366ub_8021q-reset-MAC-header-after-s.patch b/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/795-13-net-dsa-tag_rtl8366ub_8021q-reset-MAC-header-after-s.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..e3838dad57
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/795-13-net-dsa-tag_rtl8366ub_8021q-reset-MAC-header-after-s.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+From: stuoningur <50464069+stuoningur@users.noreply.github.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_rtl8366ub_8021q: reset MAC header after stripping the trap header
+
+rtl8366ub_8021q_control_rcv() strips the RTL8_4 header with
+dsa_strip_etype_header(), which moves the MAC addresses forward over
+it. skb->mac_header still points at the old frame start until
+dsa_switch_rcv() resets it after ->rcv() returns, so the following
+eth_hdr(skb)->h_proto check reads bytes 4-5 of the destination MAC.
+
+An 802.1Q tag on a trapped frame sits behind the RTL8_4 header, so the
+conduit cannot strip it into vlan_tci and this in-band check is the
+only place it is seen. A trapped frame on a management VID is thus not
+passed to dsa_8021q_rcv() and reaches the bridge still tagged.
+
+Update the MAC header right after the strip, as tag_sja1105.c does for
+the same native-header-plus-tag_8021q layout.
+
+Reported-by: dmtpascoal (https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24237)
+---
+--- a/net/dsa/tag_rtl8366ub_8021q.c
++++ b/net/dsa/tag_rtl8366ub_8021q.c
+@@ -215,6 +215,11 @@ static struct sk_buff *rtl8366ub_8021q_r
+ 		src_port = rtl8366ub_8021q_control_rcv(skb);
+ 		if (src_port < 0)
+ 			return NULL;
++		/* The RTL8_4 header strip moved the MAC addresses forward.
++		 * Update the MAC header so eth_hdr() sees the frame's real
++		 * EtherType and an in-band 802.1Q tag is found below.
++		 */
++		skb_set_mac_header(skb, -ETH_HLEN);
+ 		switch_id = netdev->dsa_ptr->ds->index;
+ 		trapped = true;
+ 	}
